notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Sansec published the original research. Censys dug into the web of compromised domains. The page lists c/side for a complete timeline and the corrected scale, and Qualys for what you need to know. The MITRE page defines T1583.001, Acquire Infrastructure: Domains, behind stage 01.

The background slides name their own sources: MITRE ATT&CK, the RFC on the web origin concept, and OWASP.

