The page names maintainership changes in packages as the mechanism behind XZ Utils and event-stream. The four topics are the page's related defense topics.
notes:
The page links two other kill chains and four defense topics.

In its defense on ownership changes, the page says the same instinct applies to maintainership changes in packages, the mechanism behind XZ Utils and event-stream. Each has its own kill chain on csoh.org.

The page's related defense topics are API and web security, CI/CD and supply chain, how csoh.org is secured, and detection engineering. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery. The page on how csoh.org is secured is where the page says csoh.org's own discipline of self-hosting and SRI is described.
